1 | devops | Fix issues 2760 and 2761 in one PR. Read BOTH issues in full first. They are grouped because both are small CI hygiene fixes in adjacent files and splitting them would cost two review cycles for no benefit. ISSUE 2760, one line. The vendored golangci-lint schema added in 2756 lives at .github/golangci/ but that path matches NO filter in .github/workflows/ci.yml, where the go filter is apps/api/** and ci_workflows is .github/workflows/**. So a commit touching ONLY the schema does not trigger Go Lint and a corrupted or over permissive schema refresh lands unverified. Add .github/golangci/** to the go filter. PROVE IT, do not assume: path filters are easy to write and easy to get silently wrong. Push a throwaway branch whose only change is to the schema file and show Go Lint RUNNING rather than skipping, and paste the run URL. Then confirm a web only change still skips the Go jobs, so you have not widened the filter into running Go on everything. ISSUE 2761, five findings against scripts/check-prd-index.py, all reproduced by the reviewer and all currently latent. F1 is the important one and is MEDIUM: the script strips HTML comments but nothing strips fenced code blocks, so a link inside a triple backtick fence still counts as a reference, which means moving a real index row into a fence leaves the gate at exit 0 with that page effectively unlisted. Fix it in the same place the HTML comment stripping already happens. F2: pages_dir.glob star dot md is not recursive, so a new unindexed spec in a subdirectory under docs/prd/pages produces exit 0, while a comment in ci.yml around lines 153 to 156 claims the gate has an opinion about exactly that case. Either make the scan recursive or correct that comment, and if you choose flat only then state the reason in the comment rather than just softening the wording. F3: the link parser splits on hash only, so a query suffix drops the link and the operator is told the page is not indexed when it is indexed with a suffix. It fails closed which is safe, but the diagnostic points at the wrong fix. F4: a comment claims inline and reference style markdown links are supported when the regex is inline only. Either correct the comment or implement what it claims, and say which you chose. F5: a future README.md or template file inside pages would be treated as a page needing an index row. Resolve it or document it as accepted with the reasoning, since the EXEMPT escape hatch is discouraged by the script own header. FOR EVERY BEHAVIOUR YOU CHANGE, add a case to the existing selftest so the fix cannot silently regress, and confirm the selftest still passes. AFTERWARDS confirm the gate still exits 0 on the clean tree and still catches BOTH original drift directions, an unindexed page and an index row naming a missing file, by reproducing both yourself. Paste every exit code captured directly rather than read after a pipe, because a pipe returns the exit code of the last command and not the one you are testing. Delete every throwaway branch and prove it with git ls-remote. Commit before you break anything. Never run git stash, which is repo global, and never run git checkout to revert, which zeroes new files unrecoverably. Run make check-ci-wiring and paste the real exit code. HOUSE STYLE, and this is not optional: do not use the long dash character anywhere in any line you add, in code, comments, commit messages or the PR body. Use a comma, a colon, parentheses or a new sentence. A previous PR in this series had one and it had to be stripped before merge. Open a PR with Closes 2760 and Closes 2761. Omit any Co-Authored-By trailer. Do not merge. | ci/2760-2761-ci-hygiene

2 | backend-critic | READ-ONLY REVIEW of the wave 1 change on branch ci/2760-2761-ci-hygiene. You are not a producer: no commits, no push, no gh pr review, no gh pr merge, no labels, no test writing. Permitted writes are a slash tmp worktree only. Record the PR head SHA at start and re-check at report; if it moved report BLOCKED with both SHAs. THE QUESTION THAT MATTERS: after these fixes, can the PRD index gate still report success while a page is unlisted, and can the golangci schema still change without Go Lint running. Answer both by RUNNING things in a throwaway worktree, not by reading the diff. FIRST, for 2761 F1, take the real 00-INDEX.md, move an actual page row inside a triple backtick fence, run the script, and confirm exit 1 naming that page. Then confirm the HTML comment case from 1567 still raises, so the new stripping did not replace the old coverage instead of adding to it. That is the specific way this fix goes wrong. SECOND, verify F2 was genuinely resolved rather than papered over: if the scan is now recursive, create a nested unindexed page and confirm exit 1; if the producer instead narrowed the ci.yml comment, read that comment and confirm it no longer claims coverage the script lacks. Either resolution is acceptable, a mismatch between them is not. THIRD, confirm the gate still exits 0 on the clean tree and still catches both original directions, since a parser change is exactly where that regresses. FOURTH, confirm the selftest gained cases for every behaviour changed and that it fails when you deliberately break one of the new behaviours, because a selftest that passes regardless is decoration. FIFTH, for 2760, verify the path filter claim by fetching the producer proof run from the API and confirming Go Lint actually RAN on a schema only commit rather than being skipped, and separately confirm a web only change still skips the Go jobs so the filter was not widened into running Go on everything. SIXTH, confirm no long dash character appears in any added line anywhere in the diff, including comments and the PR body. SEVENTH, confirm nothing outside .github/workflows/ci.yml and scripts/check-prd-index.py changed, and that apps/api/.golangci.yml and the vendored schema are untouched. Post ONE comment on issue 2340 whose first line reads CRITIC 2760 2761 CI HYGIENE, with a verdict of SAFE-TO-MERGE or BLOCK-FIX or BLOCK-ESCALATE, per-finding severity and file and line citations. No vendor names, emails, booking ids or gcloud payloads. | ci/2760-2761-ci-hygiene
